ster was necessary to  stop harm to trump's reputation leaks to  the press could be harmful to trump and  the judge concluded with no analysis  that the government leaked stories to  the press although the government  obviously denied this and she seemed to  ignore the fact that it was former  president trump who was providing almost  all of the information to the press when  these things happened in real time now  judge cannon said that trump could be  irreparably harmed because of the stigma  of potential criminal  prosecution quote frequently the public  remembers the accusation and still  suspects guilt even after an acquittal  though as many criminal defense lawyers  have pointed out including ronaldo  mariotti mark zaid and sarah azari uh  all defendants suffer reputational  damage when they are indicted um  not just this former president these  lawyers also said that they were looking  forward to citing this case on behalf of  their clients  and yes it would be good for criminal  defendants if they could have a special  master to review evidence uh seized from  them in the pre-indictment stage in all  criminal cases and they would have a  much better chance of avoiding criminal  indictment if they could identify the  government's witnesses and knew what the  government was thinking beforehand and  that's one of the reasons why the doj  opposed trump's motion for a special  master but national security lawyer  bradley moss thinks that it won't help  most criminal defendants because the  judge wrote this to help trump and trump  only now in her order judge cannon seems  to confirm moss's conclusion that the  rules are different in this particular  case quote as a function of plaintiff's  former position as president of the  united states the stigma associated with  the subject seizure is in a league of  its own and judge cannon came up with  another reason why trump might suffer  irreparable harm quote a future  indictment based to any degree on  property that 